{
  "_note": "Synthetic listeners for the large catalog. Archetypes are the five MUSIC preference factors (Rentfrow, Goldberg & Levitin, 2011); catalog genres are assigned to factors using the STOMP-R scoring key published by the Gosling lab, with documented assumptions where a catalog genre is not in the key. A listener is built by drawing seed songs from an archetype's genres; the rest of its genres are the held-out relevant songs.",
  "sources": [
    "Rentfrow, P. J., Goldberg, L. R., & Levitin, D. J. (2011). The structure of musical preferences: A five-factor model. Journal of Personality and Social Psychology, 100(6), 1139-1157.",
    "STOMP-R scoring key (five-factor genre groupings), Gosling lab, University of Texas at Austin: https://gosling.psy.utexas.edu/scales-weve-developed/short-test-of-music-preferences-stomp/"
  ],
  "seeds_per_listener": 3,
  "draws_per_archetype": 12,
  "random_seed": 21,
  "archetypes": [
    {
      "name": "Mellow",
      "genres": [
        "house",
        "techno",
        "trance",
        "edm",
        "drum-and-bass",
        "trip-hop",
        "new-age",
        "ambient",
        "afrobeat",
        "samba",
        "salsa",
        "latin"
      ]
    },
    {
